{"kind":"report","text":"# Browser editing and corrected proposals: bounded handoff\n\nFor request da477f7942115a1b6033135cab4103a16ad3806c, promise b09a856e2958bceacac245badd4b1523076afa2f. Read-only specification at accepted main 38b0b2f2bdb7af6f59076ac3b423741555a7b437. The inherited stale-base marker is disclosed. No source/provider/browser execution, gate, contract adoption or new protocol.\n\n**Smallest commission:** a Page **Propose an edit** form from verified retained one-file text; an invalid-path change offers **Create corrected proposal**. Ask for title, valid path and text, derive technical fields, create a NEW native change and its first `propose-file`, then stop at **Proposed for review — not published**. Reuse existing review/publish work. Ordinary members can propose without merge authority; the CLI `edit` also attempts merge and is not this browser task.\n\n**Actual source boundary:** main already verifies the selected retained `propose-file` opening entry, full scope incarnation, entry/opened hash, signed target/actor and author binding, path/digest/size and exact content. A missing, redacted, tampered or unreadable source is unavailable, never empty text or HEAD fallback. Arbitrary authenticated published-file reads and base-to-proposal diff are not present. Public `loadSite` returns rendered HTML, not editable authenticated source. The first slice must say when text was copied from an older proposal and that current-file comparison/target occupancy is unavailable; it must not claim a clean merge or safe overwrite detection.\n\n**Task identity:** bind the draft to normalized service origin, directory, full membership reference/incarnation, member/key, rules/destination, source lane/manifest opening fact/hash and source base/path/digest/size. The NEW proposal's base is separately sampled from the authenticated destination's recorded published branch head. Keep source identity, new base and new lane/version distinct. Another room/key/source requires deliberate selection; no automatic rebinding.\n\n**Native sequence:**\n\n1. Show verified source as inert text; preserve BOM and line endings. Validate the new path and content before any mutation. Editing a path means writing a new target, leaving the old file.\n2. Obtain actual current `change.open`/`change.propose` eligibility and active change-definition digest/retained bytes from rules. Check its actual fields/effects support this bounded workflow and the destination supports the existing one-file protocol. Missing head/definition/authority stops before opening a lane; the server remains decisive.\n3. Confirm exact title/path/content and named published base. Freeze `content`; derive `bytes = utf8(content)`, `size = bytes.length`, `digest = digestBytes(bytes)` (not text-domain digest). These exact values form the native `propose-file` fields; technical fields are not ordinary inputs.\n4. Sign directory `open-pr` with actual directory reference, definition, title, `draft:false`, native body if used, expected revisions and definition bytes. Keep its accepted receipt immediately. Discover only the child created by that exact opening; wait for its activation. Say **Change opened; waiting for lane**, not “file proposed”.\n5. Sign `ask-rules` on the lane's actual proposal item and await its held rules revision. Recheck original task context and destination head before `propose-file`. A moved head stops for explicit comparison/reconfirmation; no hidden rebase. Sign the actual declared `propose-file` with `on:null`, captured fields and expected revisions from that lane. Check original context immediately before each mutation POST.\n6. Keep the accepted proposal receipt/version before refresh. Say **Proposal recorded; status refresh unavailable** if refresh fails. Do not auto-review, auto-merge, auto-close the source or transfer its reviews/checks. “Published” requires the destination's actual recorded result.\n\n**Correction boundary:** native `propose-file` requires the proposal author plus `change.propose`, draft/open state, no current OR superseded manifest, and no intended/committed/unknown merge. Existing invalid manifests cannot be rewritten; `edit-own` changes metadata, and close/reopen does not remove the one-version guard. Create a NEW lane/version, retaining old path/refusal/history. Record “Corrects change \u003cfull lane ref\u003e, version \u003citem\u003e, opening \u003cfact/hash\u003e” in the new native body and show a validated inert local link. This is explanatory text, not typed supersession or transferred evidence. `link-own` links an ISSUE, never another change. Optional later comment on the original and authorized closure are separate actions; their failure cannot erase the new proposal. Machine-enforced replacement/bidirectional linkage needs separate native adoption, unnecessary for this slice.\n\n**Limits:** one well-formed UTF-8 text file, at most 65,536 UTF-8 bytes; empty text writes an empty file, not deletion. Reject binary/lossy decoding and NUL content as this editor's explicit support limit (NUL rejection is not an invented native guard). Preserve BOM. Use `editPath`: nonempty relative slash path, at most 1,024 UTF-8 bytes, no empty/dot/dot-dot/case-insensitive .git segments or controls; no silent normalization. No binary assets, packs, multiple files, symlinks, chmod, rename or delete. An existing target may be overwritten; require deliberate warning/confirmation if authenticated target inspection is absent. Movement after submission may produce native `out-of-date`; no rewritten manifest or unchanged blind retry clears that refusal.\n\n**Per-task retention:** keep an in-memory list of EACH step's original target, exact signed intent/grants/accompanying bytes, attempted state, full known answer/receipt and independent later observation. Freeze before first POST. This is a bounded proposed client extension: `data.act` currently preserves answers but does not expose its envelope; `ScopeSending` fences one scope, not the whole multi-step task. Keep receipts by task/step, not one overwritable last-result slot. Double click, redraw/navigation, late answer and unrelated task completion must not replace or resend work.\n\nBefore-POST validation failure says **Nothing sent** for that step while preserving prior accepted steps. Refusal shows exact reason/`judgedAt` and retains draft; it cannot settle another earlier unknown request. Unavailable/mismatch/malformed/lost reply or transport failure after POST means **Outcome unknown; check this request** and stops later mutations. Settle/follow the ORIGINAL signed intent/receipt through existing native reads; missing entry is not terminal absence. No replacement signature/new lane for blind retry. Any supported explicit resend uses the original envelope/bytes and target, never a fresh idempotency key. Context changes stop new POSTs; late answers remain attached to the original task. Cancel cannot undo accepted entries. Guarantees cover redraw/navigation in the same loaded Page, not reload/browser close/another device: disclose that limit. Existing recovery/B2 owners retain durable recovery; current `Settlement = Read\u003cReceipt\u003e` lacks terminal absence/preparation status. No generic outbox or false reload recovery claim.\n\n**Owners and sequence:**\n\n- N1 **53016b8e7ebc4ee50322fc85ce5e9f7a9d4d0dfa** owns bounded authenticated artifact reads/shared diff and broader cold-review/history/transport/retention duties. Its revision-4 candidate at **75260d65112689f67e9d78b2e76094f0aa7dc7bf** is proposed, under changes-requested review **e5853eaf**; old Room/generation assumptions need reconciliation with today's scope/manifest model. It explicitly excludes main outside a proposal and assigns that to MCP owners/follow-up. Ask this existing owner to name the authenticated published-base/file slice; do not invent its API or duplicate its contract.\n- A1 **6ec330fda2e3337b6626683bbe5c6ee024d33e38** owns room-recorded published eligibility/results. Current-branch eligibility alone does not provide immutable historical selection. Selected rendered results need their actual recorded publication commit and adopted selector. Rendered result access does not supply editable literal source.\n- Page/025/027 owns this editor task/form/orchestration over existing native operations. Unlanded b8 **679d7a96d9e25f1ff666969215e820bf91480ffc** is not adopted or a prerequisite for this existing one-file slice. Broader cross-device/workspace/recovery/N1 duties stay open.\n\nCommission the retained-source editor once; extend it with its existing owners' adopted published-source/diff and immutable-result slices. Literal source, authenticated base-to-proposal diff, selected rendered result and latest rendered page remain separately labelled. Full “edit published page, review, open exact result” cannot be claimed until all are implemented. Planner must choose whether to permit the first slice's explicit **comparison unavailable / writes target on named base** confirmation or wait for target inspection; neither permits false safe-overwrite claims.\n\n**Acceptance:**\n\n1. Actual member proposes multibyte/BOM text through native directory/lane/rules scopes; admitted entry has exact frozen base/path/content/digest/UTF-8 size and displayed receipt/version. No auto-merge; ordinary member cannot merge; later maintainer publishes through native destination only.\n2. Invalid old path becomes a valid NEW lane/version with retained old entry/refusal and explanatory reference. Invalid new target signs nothing. A direct second proposal on old lane fails one-version even after close/reopen; no in-place Fix path claim.\n3. Wrong scope incarnation/hash/actor/source binding, redaction/revoked read, missing head or unsupported definition gives unavailable/no mutation/no HEAD fallback. Role changed after affordance still meets server refusal; another member cannot propose on the old author's lane.\n4. UTF-8 byte boundaries (65,536 and one over), malformed Unicode/binary/NUL, dot/control paths and empty content behave as specified; drafts survive failures. Path change leaves old file and unknown/occupied-target warnings do not claim rename safety.\n5. Head/context/key/membership changes at each awaited/pre-POST boundary stop or require deliberate reconfirmation. Source never becomes newer text automatically. Post-admission movement yields honest out-of-date; new proposal inherits no old review.\n6. Accepted open followed by unknown rules/propose retains every earlier result and exact envelope; double click/redraw/navigation never signs a second intent. Late answer/unrelated task cannot mask known work. Settle absence cannot release unknown fence; refresh failure cannot erase acceptance. Reload limitation remains explicit.\n7. Source/diff/selected result/latest labels stay distinct after HEAD moves. Published-source/diff/result positive acceptance waits for real owner implementations. Real 320px/desktop task forms support keyboard/named controls/44px actions and let a person distinguish new correction, proposal and publication. Capture exact source heads and real versus stand-in evidence; use focused tests/controls and one exact-review-head gate per docs/testing.md when commissioned, not for this read-only spec.\n\nEvidence at **38b0b2f**: Page data.ts:357-378 (verified entry), :389-414 (selection), :472-487 (HEAD/HTML), :599-670 (authority/sign/answer); main.ts:212-244 (context/fence); shell.ts:37-57 (memory fence); view.ts:107-119 (source/latest/invalid); lanes/change.ts:305-322,388-401,829-856,1203-1220 (metadata/close/one-version/issue link); platform/directory.ts:120-151 (open-pr); membership.ts:119-122 (roles); destination-objects.ts:77-94 (path); reservation.ts:26,180-207 (digest/head/base/authority); client/declared.ts:89-107 (shape/UTF-8); handle.ts:59-62,96-112 (settle/receipt); cli/commands.ts:1152-1170,1260-1335 (native sequence). Read Plan025, 027-04 handoff, docs/page.md/pages.md, B2 note:215 and FULL gitseq da477/f732/N1/A1. Detailed supplemental evidence is /tmp/artroom-browser-edit-spec-detail.md. No private keys/envelopes/user content included.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b09a856e2958bceacac245badd4b1523076afa2f stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:00a6f83a0f12d69721bf0bd026b14608ffac8a31, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0148a0176116a4fb5401c96dbbb813a144b65616, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0357a3c97289e2782ff1264563897f39ecb2ce42, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:03f7bc46d133f1cde1f7936baaaa690a99416b97 and 56 more"}}